          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
            A basic statement in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (fundamental group of the circle is the integers)
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
              is the additive group of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_1(S^1) \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} \mathbb{Z}
            %p
              and the isomorphism is given by assigning
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/winding+number"} winding number
          %p
            Here in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+homotopy+theory"} topological homotopy theory
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} topological subspace
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msubsup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 = \{x \in \mathbb{R}^2 \,\vert\, x_1^2 + x_2^2 = 1 \} \subset \mathbb{R}^2
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+plane"} Euclidean plane
            with its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            of the same
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushout"} homotopy pushout
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo *
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mo *
                  %mo *
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S^1 \simeq \ast \underset{\ast \sqcup \ast}{\coprod} \ast
                  \\,,
          %p
            hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            that it makes a homotopy commuting diagram of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                          %mo ⊔
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\ast \sqcup \ast &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \ast
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;\swArrow&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\ast &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; S^1
                  }
                  \\,.
          %h2#proofs Proofs
          %h3#ProofInTopologicalHomotopyTheory In topological point-set homotopy theory
          %p
            We discuss the classical proof in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+topology"} point-set
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+homotopy+theory"} topological homotopy theory
          #ClassicalPointSetProof.proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/UniversalCoveringOfCircle.png", :width => "150"}/
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+covering+space"} universal covering space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{S^1}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
              (by
              = succeed "):" do
                %a{:href => "universal+covering+space#UniversalCoveringOfCircleRealLine"} this example
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi cos
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p \coloneqq (cos(2 \pi(-)), \sin(2 \pi(-)))
                    \\;\colon\; \mathbb{R}^1 \longrightarrow S^1
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+path-connected+topological+space"} locally path-connected
              (
              %a{:href => "locally+path-connected+space#LocallyPathConnectedCircle"}> this example
              ) and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-locally+simply+connected+topological+space"} semi-locally simply connected
              (
              %a{:href => "semi-locally+simply+connected+topological+space#LocallySimplyConnectedCircle"}> this example
              ) the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+covering+spaces"} fundamental theorem of covering spaces
              applies and gives that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^1
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
              equals the automorphism group of its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representation"} permutation representation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Aut
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cov
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Aut
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Fib
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Aut_{Cov(S^1)}(\mathbb{R}^1)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    Aut_{\pi_1(S^1) Set}(Fib_{S^1})
                    \\,.
            %p
              Moreover, as a corollary of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+covering+spaces"} fundamental theorem of covering spaces
              we have that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
              representation of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+covering+space"} universal covering space
              is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(S)
              on itself (
              %a{:href => "universal+covering+space#ReconstructCoveringForFreeAndTransitiveMonodromyRepresentation"}> this prop.
              ).
            %p
              But the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
              of any group regarded as an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              on itself by left multiplication is canonically isomorphic to that group itself (by
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "permutation+representation#AutomorphismsOfGAsGTorsor"} this example
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Aut
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Fib
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Aut
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Aut_{{\pi_1(S^1)} Set}(Fib_{S^1})
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    Aut_{{\pi_1(S^1)} Set}( \pi_1(S^1) )
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\pi_1(S^1)
                    \\,.
            %p Therefore to conclude the proof it is now sufficient to show that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Aut
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cov
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathrm{Aut}_{Cov(S^1)}(\mathbb{R}^1) \simeq \mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
            %p
              \# To that end, consider a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mo ≃
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{R}^1 &amp;&amp; \underoverset{\simeq}{f}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; \mathbb{R}^1
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{p}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; S^1
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in S^1
              be any point, and consider the restriction of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              to the fibers over the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi p
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∖
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mo ≃
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi p
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∖
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∖
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    p^{-1}(S^1 \setminus \{s\}) &amp;&amp; \underoverset{\simeq}{f}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; p^{-1}(S^1 \setminus \{s\})
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{p}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; S^1 \setminus \{s\}
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
              property we have (via
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "universal+covering+space#UniversalCoveringOfCircleRealLine"} this example
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Disc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p^{-1}(S^1 \setminus \{s\})
                    \\simeq
                    (0,1) \times Disc(\mathbb{Z})
                    \\,.
            %p Therefore, up to homeomorphism, the restricted function is of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Disc
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mo ≃
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Disc
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi pr
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi pr
                                  %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (0,1)\times Disc(\mathbb{Z})
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\underoverset{\simeq}{f}{\longrightarrow}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    (0,1) \times Disc(\mathbb{Z})
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{pr_1}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{pr_1}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; (0,1)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
              this means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is equivalently given by its two components
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
