          %h3#ProofInHomotopyTypeTheory In homotopy type theory
          %p
            There is also a purely synthetic a proof in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#LicataShulman13"}> Licata-Shulman 13
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#UF"} UF, corollary 8.1.10
          %h2#Consequences Consequences
          #CoveringOfCircleAndConjugacyClassesOfSymmetricGroup.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+spaces"} coverings
                of the circle are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
                in the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
              construction assigns to an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+class"} isomorphism class
              of covering spaces over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
              consisting of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              elements
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
              of elements the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(n)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mtext isomorphism classes of
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mtext finite covering spaces
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mtext over the circle
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mtext conjugacy classes of
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mtext elements of a symmetric group
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left \{
                    \\array{
                    \\text{isomorphism classes of}
                    \\\
                    \\text{finite covering spaces }
                    \\\
                    \\text{over the circle}
                    }
                    \\right\}
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\text{conjugacy classes of}
                    \\\
                    \\text{elements of a symmetric group}
                    }
                    \\right\}
            %p
              To see this, we may without restriction (via
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "groupoid#representation#GroupoidRepresentationsAreProductsOfGroupRepresentations"} this prop.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in S^1
              so that a monodromy representation is equivalently a groupoid morphism of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi ρ
                    %mi Core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho
                    \\;\colon\;
                    B \mathbb{Z}
                    \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    B \pi_1(S^1,x)
                    \\overset{\rho}{\longrightarrow}
                    Core(Set)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
              on a single generator, such as morphism is uniquely determined by the image of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \in \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{-1}(x)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon p^{-1}(x) \overset{\simeq}{\to} \{1, \cdots, n\}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Σ
