          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              %strong (three-sheeted covers of the circle)
            %p
              Consider the three-sheeted
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+spaces"} covering spaces
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            %p
              By example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoveringOfCircleAndConjugacyClassesOfSymmetricGroup"}
              these are, up to isomorphism, given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
              of the elements of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(3)
              on three elements. These in turn are labeled by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cycle"} cycle
              structure of the elements (
              %a{:href => "symmetric+group#ConjugacycClassesOfSymmetricGroupCorrespondToCycleSet"}> this prop.
              ).
            %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/The3SheetedCoveringsOfTheCircle.png", :width => "150"}/
            %p For the symmetric group on three elements there are three such classes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
